                    "# Toroidal Closure / Dimensional Stability Framework\n\n\
This notebook is a planning scaffold for a rigorous computational framework \
around **18 stable scales** of toroidal closure / dimensional stability, with \
an emphasis on symbolic structure, testability, and TypeScript export \
generation.\n\n## Scope\n\nWe will structure the project into:\n\n1. **Formal \
variables and axioms**\n2. **Derived invariants and closure metrics**\n3. \
**18 stability tests**\n4. **Wolfram Language reference implementation**\n5. \
**TypeScript computational file templates**\n6. **Validation, residual \
analysis, and precision policy**\n\n## 1. Core formal objects\n\nLet the core \
state at scale ``s`` be represented by:\n\n```wl\nstate[s_] := <|\n  \
\"ScaleIndex\" -> s,\n  \"InformationDensity\" -> rho[s],\n  \
\"FieldComplexity\" -> chi[s],\n  \"Resolution\" -> res[s],\n  \"Curvature\" \
-> kappa[s],\n  \"Torsion\" -> tau[s],\n  \"ClosurePhase\" -> theta[s],\n  \
\"ToroidalRadiusMajor\" -> rMajor[s],\n  \"ToroidalRadiusMinor\" -> \
rMinor[s],\n  \"Flux\" -> phiFlux[s],\n  \"Decoherence\" -> gamma[s],\n  \
\"BoundaryCoupling\" -> beta[s]\n|>\n```\n\nA toroidal closure descriptor:\n\n\
```wl\ntoroidalDescriptor[s_] := <|\n  \"AspectRatio\" -> \
rMajor[s]/rMinor[s],\n  \"ClosureRatio\" -> Exp[-Abs[theta[s] - 2 Pi \
Round[theta[s]/(2 Pi)]]],\n  \"CurvatureTorsionBalance\" -> 1/(1 + \
Abs[kappa[s] - tau[s]]),\n  \"FluxContainment\" -> 1/(1 + Abs[D[phiFlux[x], \
x] /. x -> s]),\n  \"BoundaryIntegrity\" -> 1/(1 + Abs[beta[s] - 1]),\n  \
\"MaintenanceFactor\" -> Exp[-gamma[s]]\n|>\n```\n\n## 2. Variational base\n\n\
Using the OPF-style layer-1 action:\n\n```wl\nactionDensity[rho_, chi_, res_] \
:= rho Log[chi] + chi res^2\n```\n\nA generalized extended action for \
toroidal stability can be explored as:\n\n```wl\nextendedActionDensity[s_] := \
\n  rho[s] Log[chi[s]] + chi[s] res[s]^2 + \n  lambda1 kappa[s]^2 + lambda2 \
tau[s]^2 + \n  lambda3 (theta[s] - 2 Pi n[s])^2 + \n  lambda4 \
(rMajor[s]/rMinor[s] - phi)^2 + \n  lambda5 gamma[s]^2\n```\n\nwith ``phi = \
(1 + Sqrt[5])/2``.\n\n## 3. Proposed 18 stable scales\n\nThese are \
placeholders for a fully refined classification. Each scale should have its \
own test vector and admissibility region.\n\n```wl\nstableScales = Range[18];\
\n```\n\nFor each scale ``s``, compute a stability record:\n\n```wl\n\
stabilityRecord[s_] := <|\n  \"Scale\" -> s,\n  \"ClosureRatio\" -> \
toroidalDescriptor[s][\"ClosureRatio\"],\n  \"CurvatureTorsionBalance\" -> \
toroidalDescriptor[s][\"CurvatureTorsionBalance\"],\n  \"FluxContainment\" -> \
toroidalDescriptor[s][\"FluxContainment\"],\n  \"BoundaryIntegrity\" -> \
toroidalDescriptor[s][\"BoundaryIntegrity\"],\n  \"MaintenanceFactor\" -> \
toroidalDescriptor[s][\"MaintenanceFactor\"]\n|>\n```\n\n## 4. Confidence \
corridor adaptation\n\nMap the confidence corridor image into symbolic \
computation:\n\n```wl\nphi = (1 + Sqrt[5])/2;\nphiInv = 1/phi;\nphiInv2 = \
1/phi^2;\n\nconfidenceCorridor[vfeNorm_, sigmaNorm_, phiCaution_: phiInv] := \
<|\n  \"CILower\" -> Max[phiInv2, 1 - vfeNorm],\n  \"CIUpper\" -> \
Min[phiCaution, 1 - sigmaNorm phiInv],\n  \"Regime\" -> Which[\n    \
Max[phiInv2, 1 - vfeNorm] > phiInv, \"Stable\",\n    Max[phiInv2, 1 - \
vfeNorm] > 0.432, \"Stress\",\n    True, \"Critical\"\n  ]\n|>\n```\n\n## 5. \
Eighteen rigorous tests\n\nEach test should be computable, falsifiable, and \
numerically checkable with residuals.\n\n```wl\ntestSuite[stateAssoc_] := <|\n\
  \"Test01_ClosurePhaseLock\" -> stateAssoc[\"ClosureRatio\"] >= phiInv2,\n  \
\"Test02_CurvatureTorsionBalance\" -> stateAssoc[\"CurvatureTorsionBalance\"] \
>= phiInv2,\n  \"Test03_FluxContainment\" -> stateAssoc[\"FluxContainment\"] \
>= phiInv2,\n  \"Test04_BoundaryIntegrity\" -> stateAssoc[\"BoundaryIntegrity\
\"] >= phiInv2,\n  \"Test05_MaintenanceFactor\" -> \
stateAssoc[\"MaintenanceFactor\"] >= phiInv2,\n  \"Test06_PositiveDensity\" \
-> True,\n  \"Test07_PositiveComplexity\" -> True,\n  \
\"Test08_PositiveResolution\" -> True,\n  \"Test09_AspectRatioBound\" -> \
True,\n  \"Test10_VariationalResidual\" -> True,\n  \
\"Test11_EigenmodeNeutrality\" -> True,\n  \"Test12_ScaleInvariance\" -> \
True,\n  \"Test13_BoundaryDualConsistency\" -> True,\n  \
\"Test14_MeasurementIntegrability\" -> True,\n  \"Test15_PrecisionConvergence\
\" -> True,\n  \"Test16_PipelineComposability\" -> True,\n  \
\"Test17_SymbolicReducibility\" -> True,\n  \"Test18_CorridorClassification\" \
-> True\n|>\n```\n\n## 6. Precision policy\n\nFor practical computation, use \
arbitrary precision aggressively, while noting that literal infinite working \
precision is not available for most numerical algorithms.\n\n```wl\n\
precisionPolicy[prec_: 100] := Block[{$MaxPrecision = prec, $MinPrecision = \
0}, prec]\n```\n\n## 7. TypeScript computational architecture\n\nSuggested \
file structure:\n\n```text\nsrc/\n  core/\n    types.ts\n    constants.ts\n   \
 state.ts\n    invariants.ts\n    corridor.ts\n    eigen.ts\n    residuals.ts\
\n    tests.ts\n    pipeline.ts\n  models/\n    toroidalClosure.ts\n    \
dimensionalStability.ts\n  io/\n    serialization.ts\n    report.ts\n  \
validation/\n    schemas.ts\n    assertions.ts\n  index.ts\n```\n\n### \
`src/core/types.ts`\n\n```ts\nexport type ScaleIndex = number;\n\nexport \
interface ScaleState {\n  scaleIndex: ScaleIndex;\n  informationDensity: \
number;\n  fieldComplexity: number;\n  resolution: number;\n  curvature: \
number;\n  torsion: number;\n  closurePhase: number;\n  toroidalRadiusMajor: \
number;\n  toroidalRadiusMinor: number;\n  flux: number;\n  decoherence: \
number;\n  boundaryCoupling: number;\n}\n\nexport interface \
StabilityDescriptor {\n  aspectRatio: number;\n  closureRatio: number;\n  \
curvatureTorsionBalance: number;\n  fluxContainment: number;\n  \
boundaryIntegrity: number;\n  maintenanceFactor: number;\n}\n\nexport \
interface ConfidenceCorridor {\n  ciLower: number;\n  ciUpper: number;\n  \
regime: \"Stable\" | \"Stress\" | \"Critical\";\n}\n```\n\n### \
`src/core/constants.ts`\n\n```ts\nexport const goldenRatio = (1 + \
Math.sqrt(5)) / 2;\nexport const goldenInverse = 1 / goldenRatio;\nexport \
const goldenInverseSquared = 1 / (goldenRatio * goldenRatio);\nexport const \
stableScaleCount = 18;\n```\n\n### `src/core/invariants.ts`\n\n```ts\nimport \
{ ScaleState, StabilityDescriptor } from \"./types\";\n\nexport function \
computeDescriptor(state: ScaleState): StabilityDescriptor {\n  const \
aspectRatio = state.toroidalRadiusMajor / state.toroidalRadiusMinor;\n  const \
phaseOffset = Math.abs(\n    state.closurePhase - 2 * Math.PI * \
Math.round(state.closurePhase / (2 * Math.PI))\n  );\n\n  return {\n    \
aspectRatio,\n    closureRatio: Math.exp(-phaseOffset),\n    \
curvatureTorsionBalance: 1 / (1 + Math.abs(state.curvature - state.torsion)),\
\n    fluxContainment: 1 / (1 + Math.abs(state.flux)),\n    \
boundaryIntegrity: 1 / (1 + Math.abs(state.boundaryCoupling - 1)),\n    \
maintenanceFactor: Math.exp(-state.decoherence)\n  };\n}\n```\n\n### \
`src/core/corridor.ts`\n\n```ts\nimport { ConfidenceCorridor } from \"./types\
\";\nimport { goldenInverse, goldenInverseSquared } from \"./constants\";\n\n\
export function confidenceCorridor(vfeNorm: number, sigmaNorm: number, \
phiCaution = goldenInverse): ConfidenceCorridor {\n  const ciLower = \
Math.max(goldenInverseSquared, 1 - vfeNorm);\n  const ciUpper = \
Math.min(phiCaution, 1 - sigmaNorm * goldenInverse);\n\n  const regime = \
ciLower > goldenInverse\n    ? \"Stable\"\n    : ciLower > 0.432\n      ? \
\"Stress\"\n      : \"Critical\";\n\n  return { ciLower, ciUpper, regime };\n\
}\n```\n\n### `src/core/tests.ts`\n\n```ts\nimport { StabilityDescriptor } \
from \"./types\";\nimport { goldenInverseSquared } from \"./constants\";\n\n\
export interface TestResult {\n  name: string;\n  passed: boolean;\n  value: \
number | boolean;\n  threshold?: number;\n}\n\nexport function \
runCoreTests(descriptor: StabilityDescriptor): TestResult[] {\n  return [\n   \
 {\n      name: \"ClosurePhaseLock\",\n      passed: descriptor.closureRatio \
>= goldenInverseSquared,\n      value: descriptor.closureRatio,\n      \
threshold: goldenInverseSquared\n    },\n    {\n      name: \
\"CurvatureTorsionBalance\",\n      passed: \
descriptor.curvatureTorsionBalance >= goldenInverseSquared,\n      value: \
descriptor.curvatureTorsionBalance,\n      threshold: goldenInverseSquared\n  \
  },\n    {\n      name: \"FluxContainment\",\n      passed: \
descriptor.fluxContainment >= goldenInverseSquared,\n      value: \
descriptor.fluxContainment,\n      threshold: goldenInverseSquared\n    },\n  \
  {\n      name: \"BoundaryIntegrity\",\n      passed: \
descriptor.boundaryIntegrity >= goldenInverseSquared,\n      value: \
descriptor.boundaryIntegrity,\n      threshold: goldenInverseSquared\n    },\n\
    {\n      name: \"MaintenanceFactor\",\n      passed: \
descriptor.maintenanceFactor >= goldenInverseSquared,\n      value: \
descriptor.maintenanceFactor,\n      threshold: goldenInverseSquared\n    }\n \
 ];\n}\n```\n\n## 8. Immediate next steps\n\n1. Define the exact meaning of \
the **18 stable scales**.\n2. Decide whether the scales are logarithmic, \
geometric, topological, or spectral.\n3. Formalize the toroidal closure \
operator.\n4. Derive a linearized operator and compute its \
[Eigensystem](paclet:ref/Eigensystem).\n5. Add residual-based validation and \
convergence tests.\n6. Export the TypeScript files automatically from Wolfram \
Language.\n\n## 9. Recommended Wolfram Language export generator\n\n```wl\n\
tsFiles = <|\n  \"src/core/constants.ts\" -> \"export const goldenRatio = (1 \
+ Math.sqrt(5)) / 2;\\n\",\n  \"src/index.ts\" -> \"export * from \
'./core/constants';\\n\"\n|>;\n\nKeyValueMap[\n  \
Export[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], #1}], #2, \"String\"] &,\n  tsFiles\
\n]\n```\n\n## 10. Research checklist\n\n- Define the toroidal closure metric \
tensor.\n- Specify admissible state domains.\n- Prove or test closure under \
scale recursion.\n- Derive 18 named tests with symbolic and numeric forms.\n- \
Build a WL-to-TS export pipeline.\n- Add notebook-driven reports and \
machine-readable JSON snapshots.\n\nIf you want, the next iteration can \
generate:\n\n1. a **full 18-test mathematical specification**,\n2. a \
**Wolfram Language implementation notebook**,\n3. or a **complete TypeScript \
project skeleton**.",
