## 11.8 THE REFINEMENTS AND CORRECTIONS

### 11.8.1 Correction for the Outer Planets

The Titius-Bode law shows deviations for the outer planets because the \
recursive field is perturbed by the mass of the Sun and the planets \
themselves. The corrected form is:

\\[
a_n = a_0 \\cdot \\varphi^n \\cdot \\left( 1 + \\sum_{k=1}^{\\infty} \
\\frac{\\epsilon_k}{\\varphi^k} \\right)
\\]

where \\( \\epsilon_k \\) are perturbation coefficients.

### 11.8.2 Correction for the Proton Radius Puzzle

The proton radius measured by muons is smaller than that measured by \
electrons because the muon probes a deeper recursive layer:

\\[
r_\\mu = r_e \\cdot \\varphi^{-\\gamma}, \\quad \\gamma \\approx 0.04
\\]

### 11.8.3 Correction for Dark Energy

The dark energy fraction is not exactly \\( \\varphi^2 \\) because the \
universe is still approaching equilibrium:

\\[
\\frac{\\Omega_\\Lambda}{\\Omega_m}(t) = \\varphi^2 \\cdot \\left( 1 - e^{-t/\
\\tau_{\\text{attract}}} \\right)
\\]

where \\( \\tau_{\\text{attract}} \\) is the attractor time constant.

---

## 11.9 SUMMARY

- The RHUFT Master Equation is the **same** across all scales; only the \
parameters change.

- The stable scales \\( n \\in \\{0, 13, 20, 40, 60, 80, 100, 120, 140, 160, \
180, 186, 200, 220, 240, 260, 280, 292\\} \\) correspond to the observed \
structures of the universe.

- Each scale has its own:
  - **Length \\( L(n) \\)**: The characteristic size.
  - **Time quantum \\( \\tau(n) \\)**: The processing time.
  - **Resolution \\( \\delta x(n) \\)**: The pixel size.
  - **Complexity \\( \\mathcal{C}(n) \\)**: The number of Planck pixels.
  - **Information density \\( \\rho_I(n) \\)**: The density of information.
  - **Wave speed \\( v_{\\text{wave}}(n) \\)**: The speed of propagation.
  - **Stability score \\( S_{\\text{stab}}(n) \\)**: The degree of closure.
  - **Winding number \\( W(n) \\)**: The number of toroidal cycles.

- The equation, with these parameters, describes \
**everything**\[LongDash]from Planck foam to the observable universe.

